course: dictionary
lesson: 13168
title: Fourfold
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fourfold means four times as much or as many. To find a fourfold amount, multiply by 4. A fourfold increase from 10 gives 40, because 10 × 4 = 40.
explain: «The number of visitors rose fourfold in one year.» The word rose tells you the number went up, and fourfold tells you by how much: four times as many. If there were 100 visitors, there are now 400.
explain: Fourfold can also mean having four parts or four kinds. Check the words around it. If the sentence talks about how much something has grown, it means four times as much. If it talks about parts or kinds, it means four of them.
fact: «Fourfold» means four times as much or as many.
fact: «A fourfold increase» from 10 gives 40, because 10 × 4 = 40.
fact: «Fourfold» can also mean having four parts or four kinds.
fact: «Fourfold» is used as an adjective, as in «a fourfold increase», and as an adverb, as in «rise fourfold».
fact: In science and news, «fourfold» often describes how much something has grown: «rise fourfold» means it became four times bigger.
exercise: The shop's sales rose fourfold in one month. What happened to the sales? | Sales stayed the same | Sales were cut in half | Sales were four pounds | *Sales became four times bigger
exercise: What is a fourfold increase from 5? | 9 | 54 | 15 | *20
exercise: Ben says «fourfold» means two of something. What does it really mean? | A large pile | *Four times as much or as many | Five parts | Two of something
test: A plant is 3 cm tall. It grows fourfold. How tall is it now? | 9 cm | 3 cm | 7 cm | *12 cm
test: Which sentence uses «fourfold» correctly? | *The cost rose fourfold in one year | We ate fourfold yesterday | She fourfolded her shoes | The cake was fourfold sweet
exam: A team of 3 children grows fourfold in size. How many children are in the team now? | *12 | 7 | 3 | 9
